<title>GERMANY: Bomb scare forces German plane to land in Bulgaria.</title>
<headline>Bomb scare forces German plane to land in Bulgaria.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A bomb scare forced a German airliner flying from Istanbul to Frankfurt to make an emergency landing in Sofia but no device was found, German airport officials said on Monday.</p>
<p>The Airbus A-320, which was carrying about 100 passengers, landed in Sofia on Sunday after a telephoned bomb threat.</p>
<p>The officials said Bulgarian authorities searched the plane, operated by the Aero Lloyd airline, after evacuating the passengers and crew.</p>
<p>The plane was later allowed to continue to Frankfurt.</p>
</text>
